Day 52 - Copy List with Random Pointer

Problem Statement:
A linked list of length n is given where each node contains a next pointer and an additional random pointer. The random pointer can point to any node in the list or null.

Construct a deep copy of the linked list using exactly n brand new nodes. The next and random pointers of the copied nodes must point only to nodes in the copied list.

Code

class Solution {
public:
    Node* copyRandomList(Node* head) {
        if (head == NULL) return NULL;


        unordered_map<Node*, Node*> m;


        // Create head
        Node* newhead = new Node(head->val);
        m[head] = newhead;


        Node* oldTemp = head->next;
        Node* newTemp = newhead;


        // First pass: create nodes and next pointers
        while (oldTemp != NULL) {
            Node* copyNode = new Node(oldTemp->val);
            m[oldTemp] = copyNode;


            newTemp->next = copyNode;
            newTemp = newTemp->next;


            oldTemp = oldTemp->next;
        }


        // Second pass: assign random pointers
        oldTemp = head;
        newTemp = newhead;


        while (oldTemp != NULL) {
            if (oldTemp->random != NULL)
                newTemp->random = m[oldTemp->random];
            else
                newTemp->random = NULL;


            oldTemp = oldTemp->next;
            newTemp = newTemp->next;
        }


        return newhead;
    }
};





Time Complexity:
O(n)

Space Complexity:
O(n)

Approach:
This solution uses an unordered_map to maintain a mapping between each original node and its corresponding copied node. In the first pass, all new nodes are created and their next pointers are connected, while storing the mapping in the hash map. In the second pass, the random pointer of each copied node is assigned using the map. This ensures that every random pointer in the copied list points to a new copied node, never to an original node.
